From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:19:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web-app: optionally hold Send while the grammar checker still
 underlines issues

Experimental switch "Check spelling before sending" (grammarCheckBlocksSend,
off by default, needs the grammar checker of the LanguageTool patch). While
the composer's checker underlines anything that is neither fixed nor ignored,
a send attempt (button, send key; edits too) doesn't send but opens a tip
above the send button that says why. The tip also shows on hover and focus.

Sending anyway: Ctrl/Cmd+click, the tip's "Send anyway" button, or the send
key a second time while the tip is open. Editing the text closes the tip.

The button is aria-disabled rather than disabled, which would swallow the
hover and the click. LanguageTool reports its underline count up through
onIssueCount; the count is what is underlined right now, so text typed and
sent within the checker's debounce still goes out unchecked.

Strings are in packages/web-app/fork-strings.json; covered by
scripts/test-grammar-check-e2e.mjs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
